## Copper's PulseAudio graph.
##
## The stock /etc/pulse/default.pa loads the detector that needs a running udev
## daemon. Copper's default init runs no udev, so that detector finds no card and
## every client -- firefox, mpv, cava -- is handed auto_null: cava draws bars
## from that sink's monitor while the video is silent, and Discord sees no
## microphone because there is no capture source at all.
##
## module-detect reads /proc/asound/devices instead, which the kernel fills in
## whether or not userspace has udev. It creates a sink for every playback device
## and a source for every capture device. That is the detector this image needs.

load-module module-native-protocol-unix

## A machine with no card must still have a graph for clients to attach to.
load-module module-null-sink sink_name=copper_null sink_properties=device.description="Copper Null (no sound card)"

.nofail
load-module module-detect
.fail

## Start on the null devices until copper-audio has seen which real ones
## module-detect created and repointed the defaults with pactl. Both launchers
## call copper-audio init as soon as the server is up.
set-default-sink copper_null
set-default-source copper_null.monitor
